cancelTransportPart [SimTalk]
Cancels each and every transport of the parts, which you started with the method transportPart, and
which are scheduled to be carried by the Worker designated by <Path>.
Remarks
If one part or several parts are scheduled to be transported, Plant Simulation deletes this reservation and
the Worker either walks to the WorkerPool or to his base.
If you specified a Station at which the Worker picks up finished parts, Plant Simulation deletes this
reservation as well. As soon as the Worker has picked up a part and transported it, the reservation cannot
be canceled though.
Note
If you specified a Destination when ordering the Worker to transport parts, and the Destination was
then saved in the parts to be transported, Plant Simulation does not undo this change. This means that
the specified Destination is retained and you can still query it with the attribute Destination.
Note
cancelTransportPart only cancels each and every transport of the parts, which you started with the
method transportPart.
It does not cancel automatically mediated transports initiated by a combination of the Transport
Importer and the Broker.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.cancelTransportPart -> boolean
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
true if all transport processes could be canceled.
false if they could not be canceled.
cancelTransportPart [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3199
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

false might be returned if no orders exist to transport parts or if the Worker picked up at least one part to
be transported.
Example
.Resources.MyWorker:1.cancelTransportPart
