getRouteLength [SimTalk] - Worker
Returns the route of the Worker designated by <Path> from his present location to this destination object.
Remarks
If you enter a station as the destination object, the method returns the length of the route to the
Workplace which can be reached on the shortest route.
If the Worker is exporting a service at the moment, it only takes those Workplaces into consideration,
which support the service, including all Workplaces, which are not restricted to certain services.
If you enter a Workplace as destination object, Plant Simulation always computes the length to this
Workplace, no matter if it supports the exported service or not.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getRouteLength(Target:path[, byref FoundWorkplace:object]) → length
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Target of data type path designates the destination object. The destination object can be
a Workplace, a WorkerPool, or a work station to which you attached Workplaces.
• The optional local variable FoundWorkplace of data type object is the variable into which Plant
Simulation writes the Workplace which it found at the destination object.
This is helpful if you assign a work station to the parameter Target instead of a Workplace.
Return Value
The return value has the data type length.
Is -1 if Plant Simulation did not find a route.
getRouteLength [SimTalk] - Worker
11-3202 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Examples
print .Resources.Worker:1.getRouteLength(MyWorkplace1)
var FoundWorkplace: object
.Resources.Worker:1.getRouteLength(MyStation, FoundWorkplace)
print FoundWorkplace
