getServices [SimTalk] - Worker
Returns all services of the Worker designated by <Path> and writes them into a table.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getServices(Services:table)
Parameter
The parameter Services of data type table designates the name of an unformatted table (a table in a Frame
or a local table) with three columns:
• Column 1 has the data type string and contains the Name of the Service.
• Column 2 has the data type integer and contains the Priority.
• Column 3 has the data type integer and contains the Efficiency.
Example
print .Resources.Worker:1.getServices(MyServicesTable)
