goTo [SimTalk]
Sends the Worker designated by <Path> to the designated Workplace.
Remarks
If the Worker is interrupted, but must teleport to reach the intended destination, the Worker does not
accept the order and the method returns false.
If the specified object is not a Workplace but a work station, the Worker walks to the closest Workplace
assigned to the work station instead.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.goTo(Workplace:object[, ReserveExclusively:boolean:=true]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Workplace of data type object designates the Workplace to which you want to send the
Worker.
• The optional parameter ReserveExclusively of data type boolean sets if the Workplace will be reserved
exclusively for the Worker until he leaves the Workplace (true or no parameter). In this case the
Workplace is not available any longer for another Worker, even while the designated Worker is on his
way to the Workplace. If the Workplace is already occupied by another Worker, the Worker you sent
stops and goTo returns false.
If you specify false, the Workplace is not going to be reserved. The Worker walks to the Workplace,
and if the Workplace is occupied, he waits until it becomes available again.
Note
If AutomaticMediation is deactivated and goTo is called if the parameter ReserveExclusively is true,
meaning that it reserves the Workplace, Plant Simulation checks if the Workplace still has available
Capacity. If all places of the Workplace are either occupied or reserved, Plant Simulation shows an
error message.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is true.
goTo [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3205
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
false if the Worker is exporting a service at the moment. The Worker then stays where he is currently at.
Examples
.Resources.MyWorker:1.goTo(MyWorkplace)
.Resources.MyWorker:1.goTo(MyWorkplace,false)
SimTalk
