transportPart [SimTalk]
Makes the Worker designated by <Path> transport a single part from its current location to the specified
destination. Transports several parts from the current location to their specified destination.
Remarks
Instead of one or several parts you can also specify a material flow object, which provides parts to be
picked up. Then the Worker picks up all parts, which are ready to exit and carries them away when the
Worker arrives at the specified Station until his Capacity is exhausted.
If no parts are ready to exit when the Worker arrives, Plant Simulation shows an error message.
If you do not specify a Destination, the part/the parts must already have a Destination. Plant Simulation
saves the specified Destination in the part/the parts. You can query it with the attribute Destination.
Note
The Worker can only transport several parts if he can pick all parts up at the same location.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.transportPart(PartOrStationOrParts:object/object[ ][, 
Destination:object]) -> void
<Path>.transportPart(Part:object[, Destination:object]) -> void
<Path>.transportPart(Parts:object[ ][, Destination:object]) -> void
<Path>.transportPart(Station:object[, Destination:object]) -> void
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Part of data type object designates the part that is to be transported.
• The parameter Parts of data type object designates an array of parts that are to be transported.
• The parameter Station of data type object designates the Station at which the Worker picks up the parts
that are ready to exit and carries them away.
The Station can be any material flow object that provide parts to be picked up.
• The optional parameter Destination of data type object designates the destination object to which the
Worker transports the part. If you do not specify the destination, you have to define a destination for
each part to be transported.
transportPart [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3213
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Return Value
The method does not have a return value.
It outputs error messages, which might cause the method to fail, because:
• The specified Worker is a class object.
• The specified Worker is brokered automatically.
• The specified Worker cannot transport parts.
• The specified Worker already carries a part.
• The number of parts to be carried is greater than the current Capacity of the Worker.
• The part does not exist or does not have the correct object type.
• The Destination does not exist or does not have the correct object type.
• You did not specify a Destination and the part/the parts do not have a Destination of their own.
• The part itself, that is to be transported, has a defined Destination, which differs from the specified
Destination.
• The parts to be transported have to be picked up at different locations.
• The part or one of the parts is already being transported by a Worker.
• No parts are to be picked up and carried away at the Station by the Worker.
• An error occurred while sending the Worker for picking up or transporting the parts.
Examples
waituntil .Resources.Worker:1.HasOrder = false
.Resources.Worker:1.transportPart(Station.cont, Station1)
SimTalk
